  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves developing a simplified microblogging platform, inspired by Twitter. The application focuses on core functionalities, providing a straightforward user experience.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to enable users to interact by posting tweets, following other users, and managing personal profiles. The system emphasizes simplicity while ensuring essential features are available.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- End Users: Individuals who will register, post tweets, and interact with other users.\n- Developers: Those responsible for building and maintaining the platform.\n- Administrators: Personnel who may manage user accounts and moderate content.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. View Timeline\n   - Users can view a timeline consisting of tweets from followed accounts.\n\n2. Post New Tweet\n   - Users can create and post new tweets, including the option to attach images.\n\n3. Follow/Unfollow User\n   - Users can follow or unfollow other accounts to curate their timeline content.\n\n4. Edit User Profile\n   - Users can update their profile information including their display name and email.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system should ensure data integrity and consistency through relational database constraints.\n- The platform should be user-friendly, focusing on ease of navigation and minimalistic design.\n- Security measures, such as password encryption, should be implemented to protect user data.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0042\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `bio` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_image_url` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `username` (`username`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tweets` (\n  `tweet_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` varchar(280) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tweet_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tweets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `follows` (\n  `follower_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `followee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`follower_id`, `followee_id`),\n  KEY `followee_id` (`followee_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `follows_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`follower_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `follows_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`followee_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
